  "notes": "Built from the official PSU Suggested Academic Plan (MATH 140/141 calculus track). Pre-med at Penn State is not a stand-alone flowchart major like CMPSC \u2014 it is the Premedicine B.S. (Plan Code PM_BS), which bundles the AAMC-aligned science core with breadth requirements. 'Supporting Course (Area of Concentration)' and 'Healthcare Internship' slots follow the bulletin's advising note to consult a Premedical Professional Program adviser for specific electives. 'etm' marks the core science-sequence gateway courses (Bio/Chem/Calc) that everything downstream depends on. Post-parens-fix re-scrape (AND/OR prereq-parsing bug fix) revealed CHEM 110's real prereq is MATH 22 (previously empty) -- MATH 140/141 (this plan's own Calc I/II track) do NOT substitute for it -- and MATH 22 itself real-chains through MATH 21, MATH 4, and MATH 3, none of which were in the plan. Added the real chain explicitly: MATH 3 (Semester 1), MATH 4 (Semester 2), MATH 21 (Semester 3), MATH 22 (Semester 4) -- same convention used for LSCPE/ABSM/MATSCI's identical gap. UNLIKE every other major this session, this one genuinely cannot be squeezed back into 8 terms by raising max_credits_per_semester: the bottleneck here is chain LENGTH, not per-term credit capacity. The real sequential critical path is MATH 3 -> MATH 4 -> MATH 21 -> MATH 22 -> CHEM 110 -> CHEM 112 -> CHEM 210 -> CHEM 212 -> BMB 401 (needs CHEM 210 AND CHEM 212 both) -> BMB 402 (needs BMB 401) -- ten strictly sequential terms at an absolute minimum, regardless of credit load per term. Tried bumping the cap to 18/19/20 and it made no difference (confirmed empirically) -- left at the original 17 since a higher cap doesn't help and would misrepresent the real constraint. This means CHEM 110 can no longer land in Semester 1 (it now needs the full MATH chain first, landing in Semester 5 instead), and BMB 401/402 land in Semesters 9-10. Two tests in tests.py now hard-code the old (pre-fix, incorrect) assumption that this plan finishes in exactly 8 terms with CHEM 110 in term 1 -- both are now genuinely stale given the corrected real prereq data and need a human decision (extend the plan's own modeled length to 10 terms / 5 years, or find PSU's actual official workaround for this \u2014 e.g. an ALEKS placement exemption the scraper can't see \u2014 neither of which this fix should guess at): test_full_plan_reaches_graduation_in_four_years (asserts 8 terms, warnings==[], goal met) and test_chem_lab_pairs_with_lecture_same_term (asserts CHEM 110 in term 1).",
  "max_credits_per_semester": 17,
